          <change when="2019-11-02T13:34:52-04:00" who="https://papyri.info/editor/users/t_m_hickey">Submit - Ed. pr. proposes that διοικ( ) is an error, claiming that there is a gap between δι and the rest of the word, and that the scribe therefore must have been thinking of the διὰ in l. 7. But there is no gap on the digital image (iota is just faint; it is not ligatured with delta, cf. δι- in l. 7), and διοικ(ητοῦ) is a valid reading. </change>
